WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.530
It was New York City in the 1960s, and the
city was lit up with color and life 24 hours

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:07.530
a day.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.910
From the Mad Men of the Madison Avenue advertising
companies, with their crisp pressed suits,

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.060
slick haircuts, and even slicker salesmanship,
to the revolutionary art and culture of Greenwich

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.640
Village, it was the place to be.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.400
From dusk until dawn, then all throughout
the day, the streets were positively flooded

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.970
with people on their way to work, heading
out for a night on the town, or looking to

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.570
get into some trouble.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:38.390
It wasn’t likely that you would notice one
man keeping to himself, his hands in his pockets,

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:43.430
the brim of his hat pulled low over his forehead
and casting a shadow over his eyes.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.200
Unless, of course, you were looking for him.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.079
You see, this particular man had caught the
attention of a particularly unsavory group

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:52.290
of fellows.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.129
The Di Mauro crime family was not the sort
of group you wanted to get on the bad side

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:00.650
of, especially the family’s eldest son,
Mario Di Mauro.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:05.580
And unfortunately for this quiet man in the
slate gray suit, keeping his head down, he

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.600
had found himself smack dab in the middle
of Mario’s bad side.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.070
He hadn’t done anything wrong, really.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:16.740
He’d been walking by a bakery a few days
prior, when he bumped into a little old lady

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.740
by mistake.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.880
He didn’t mean to bump her, he didn’t
mean to make her stumble, and he certainly

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.430
didn’t intend to make her drop the birthday
cake she was holding, but it all happened

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.770
just the same.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.770
The cake box fell to the ground, the cardboard
crumpled, and suddenly there was vanilla sponge

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:37.210
and buttercream frosting splattered all over
the filthy city sidewalk.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.329
The strange man helped the little old lady
back up to her feet, and apologized for the

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:45.049
trouble as she cried that her son’s 30th
birthday was ruined.

00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:50.189
He watched her adjust her hat and run away,
and felt a pang of regret, but soon forgot

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:53.290
all about the cake, the lady, the birthday.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.110
Mario didn’t.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.039
His friends called him Mario “Birthday Boy”
Di Mauro for a reason.

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:05.130
All year he looked forward to one thing: his
favorite cake, from his favorite bakery, delivered

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.490
to him by his favorite person, his mother.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:13.070
When Mrs. Di Mauro described the stranger
who had caused her to drop the cake, Mario

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:19.750
decided that this disrespect, to him, to his
mother, to his entire family, would not go

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.110
unpunished.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:25.710
He sent out a group of his favorite lackeys,
Bobby “The Weasel” Passarella, Vernon

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.230
“Two-Knife” Galletti, and Ben “The Mammoth”
Santoni.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:34.360
They tracked the man down, figured out his
usual haunts, his schedule, the streets he

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.500
walked down every day, and reported back.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.390
Mario gave the order, it was time to make
their move.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:47.580
And so, on that ordinary day as that nice,
neat, polite man walked down the street, his

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.340
cake mistake far from his mind, Mario and
the boys watched from the shadows.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.060
Ordinarily, Mario wouldn’t involve himself
directly in this kind of nasty business.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.230
He would send others to do his dirty work.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:04.860
But this was personal, and he wanted to be
there to see the look on this disrespectful

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.360
stranger’s face as he learned his lesson.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.900
The men trailed him all day, waiting until
it was dark, until the man was alone.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.120
Then, and only then, they would strike.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.460
Curiously, the man never did much of anything
other than walk around the city, avoiding

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.460
others.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:24.760
If someone spoke to him, asked him for directions,
he would answer them courteously, but then

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.580
he would continue on his way.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.940
Once, he stopped at a restaurant for a steak
and a glass of water, but he seemed to have

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.140
no job, no family, no friends, or really much
of a life at all.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.230
Though the others were perplexed, Mario was
delighted.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.050
There was no one to miss this man once he
was gone.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.170
This would be even easier than he had expected.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:51.080
As the streets grew darker and the night deepened,
the mobsters prepared to execute their attack.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:56.890
Armed with knives, guns, piano wire, and all
their trusty usual suspects, they were poised

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.070
for the perfect moment.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.220
And the perfect moment had arrived.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.610
The strange man turned down an alley, and
the group followed him into the shadows.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.990
They were just about to corner him, when the
man turned around and faced them.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:14.090
“Excuse me, gentlemen,” the man spoke
in a clipped voice, refined but cold, with

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.940
an accent none of them could quite place.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.390
“Would you care to explain why you’ve
been following me all day?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.100
It’s becoming a bit unsettling.”

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.440
The group froze, shocked.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.360
What kind of game was this guy playing?

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.550
“Listen here, wise guy,” Vernon said,
holding one of his signature two knives in

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:31.550
each hand.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.600
“We don’t take kindly to folks with bad
manners.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.110
We thought we’d give you a good old-fashioned
etiquette lesson.”

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.610
“Have we met?”

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.280
the strange man asked, perplexed.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:47.500
“No, but we’re about to become well acquainted,”
Vernon took a step forward, the blades glinting

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.290
menacingly in the limited light.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:53.280
There was nothing behind his target but a
closed off alleyway.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.560
Nowhere to run.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.810
“I don’t think you want to do that,”
the man held his hands up in a gesture of

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.810
peace.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:01.960
“Please, it would be a terrible idea.”

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:02.960
Vernon laughed.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.210
“Would ya get a load of this clown?”

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.060
Ben shrugged his massive shoulders, and cracked
his knuckles.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.420
Bobby wound the sharp piano wire around his
fists, ready to wrap it around the stranger’s

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.420
neck.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.420
“Enough small talk.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.820
Gut him, Vernon,” Mario called out, stepping
forward to get a better look at his intended

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:20.820
victim.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.510
“I’ve had just about enough of this.”

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.760
At his boss’s word, Vernon rushed at the
stranger, stabbing him in the stomach.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:30.750
Suddenly, he cried out, one of his knives
falling to the ground with a clatter.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.610
He grabbed at his own abdomen, stumbling back
as blood poured between his fingers.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.190
“He cut me!”

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.250
“With what?!”

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.300
called Ben.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:42.450
“I tried to warn you…” the stranger
sighed, almost sounding disappointed that

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.330
no one had listened to him.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.670
“Forget it, I’ll handle this.”

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.780
Bobby grabbed ahold of the stranger, pulling
the piano wire tight across his throat.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:54.320
No sooner had the wire tightened across the
man’s windpipe, then Bobby was on his knees

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.291
on the ground, clawing at his own throat as
he gasped for air.

00:05:57.291 --> 00:06:03.510
A thin line of blood trickled down his neck,
there something invisible, small, and sharp

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.030
had cut into the skin.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:09.180
Ben rushed to the side of his fallen brethren,
picking them up in his massive arms and pulling

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.360
them back out of the way.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:15.850
“I guess if you want something done right,
you’ve gotta do it yourself,” Mario said,

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:20.100
pulling his favorite pistol out of his pocket
and aiming it directly between the stranger’s

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.100
eyes.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.750
“Please, you don’t want to do this…”
the stranger begged, but Mario wouldn’t

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.750
yield.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.230
“Oh, I very much do.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:29.950
Call it a belated birthday present.”

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.360
And he pulled the trigger.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:36.250
When the police arrived to investigate the
sound of gunshots, they found a bizarre sight:

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:41.500
Four gangsters, lying dead on the ground from
a gunshot wound, choking, stabbing, and a

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.820
heavy blow to the head.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:47.230
At the center of it all, there was one man,
completely unharmed except for a hole in his

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.550
shirt and some dirt on his suit.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:53.810
Unsure what else to do with the situation,
they arrested the man and brought him in for

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:54.810
questioning.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:59.200
The murder suspect had no identification on
him, and refused to give the officers a full

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.200
name.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.090
So, they threw him in a holding cell and designated
him a John Doe.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:06.690
They questioned the man for hours, trying
to get him to explain how he had taken down

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:11.140
four of the city’s deadliest gangsters without
getting a scratch on him, or where he had

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:14.470
managed to stash his weapons before the police
got there.

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:17.050
Every time, he insisted: “I never touched
them.”

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:21.710
At this same time, the SCP Foundation was
combing their way through arrest records,

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:25.550
looking for any signs of the strange and unusual
passing through police custody.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:30.669
They paid particular attention to John and
Jane Doe’s, looking for people with superhuman

00:07:30.669 --> 00:07:33.370
abilities or unexplained characteristics.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:37.540
The events in New York City caught their eye,
and a Foundation operative was dispatched

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.490
to retrieve the strange man from the NYPD.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:45.710
They found him sitting in his cell, reading
a newspaper, refusing to answer any more questions.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:49.510
When the operative noticed a large bruise
on the attending officer’s face, he stammered

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:55.030
“The guy wasn’t cooperating…I tried
to show him I was serious, but this happened.”

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.290
“He hit you?”

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.380
The operative asked.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.080
The policeman simply shook his head.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.080
“No.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.080
I don’t know how he does it.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.500
I hit him!”

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.950
The man was released into the custody of the
SCP Foundation, and officially designated

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.710
SCP-073.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:12.650
SCP-073
is a man of Middle Eastern descent, standing

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:16.930
at 6’1” tall, with black hair and blue
eyes.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:21.400
He appears to be in his early thirties, but
research indicates that he is much older than

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.400
that.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.180
He looks like an average man, with a few notable
exceptions.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:29.690
His arms, legs, spinal cord, and shoulder
blades have been replaced with metal of some

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.690
kind.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:34.280
When asked about these metal additions, the
subject seems surprised, and insists that

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.440
he has no memory of when or why the alterations
were made.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.160
He has a symbol carved into his forehead which
has not yet been translated, though it seems

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.240
to be Sumerian in origin.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:48.500
The subject is aware of the symbol’s presence
but does not like to discuss it at all.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:52.690
He becomes distressed whenever it is brought
up and refuses to explain.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:57.600
SCP-073 has the needs of an ordinary human
being and requires regular consumption of

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.810
meals as well as plenty of water.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:04.800
He subsists on a strictly animal-based diet
of various meats and cheeses, which are provided

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.100
for him on demand.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:11.130
He refers to himself as Cain and is generally
friendly and polite to everyone he interacts

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.430
with, if a bit formal and stiff.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:17.640
He is extremely helpful and has volunteered
to help out with various tasks around the

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:22.000
Foundation site, from cleaning and general
maintenance to assisting in research.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.740
He prefers to provide assistance on the research
side of things, largely due to his photographic

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.750
memory, wide knowledge of world history, and
fluency in most of the world’s common spoken

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.760
languages.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.779
When he was first brought in to Foundation
custody, he provided evidence of these skills

00:09:36.779 --> 00:09:43.820
via a placement test in French, German, English,
Japanese, Mandarin, Italian, and a dozen other

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:48.400
languages, a trivia contest where he bested
the Foundation’s top historian, and a memory

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:54.350
exam wherein he read an entire eight-hundred-page
dictionary in a minute and a half and was

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:57.230
able to recite every single word without help.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:01.980
In addition to his intelligence, and some
of the unusual aspects of his appearance,

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:06.010
the subject also possesses some impressive
and strange abilities.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:11.720
Cain’s physical presence is deadly to any
life grown in soil, from fruits and vegetables

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.990
to trees, grass, and anaerobic bacteria.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:19.950
Any soil that Cain sets foot on will experience
this effect, which extends to all land in

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.730
a twenty-meter radius.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:27.180
Cain also has a destructive impact on plant-based
material that has undergone processing, including

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.440
paper and wood, and on produce that has been
grown hydroponically.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.540
It is unknown why his presence has this effect,
but it influences everything from his diet

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.460
to the furniture placed in his containment
chamber.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:43.910
Cain is impervious to physical harm, which
is not out of the ordinary for an anomaly

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:49.540
in the custody of the SCP Foundation, but
the way in which this invulnerability manifests

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.740
is particularly notable.

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:57.280
Any violence that is directed toward Cain
bounces off him and turns back on his attacker.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:01.150
Whatever is done to him will affect the person
attempting to hurt him.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:06.000
This applies whether a person means harm or
not, and whether they use a weapon or their

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.340
bare hands.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:11.980
Though the harm done to Cain does not show
up as a physical injury, he does still experience

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:16.440
the sensation of pain, and has requested that
the Foundation refrain from any especially

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:21.950
painful tasks - especially since he has been
so cooperative with their research.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:26.470
SCP-073’s resistance to any physical damage
has made it difficult for the Foundation to

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.230
perform any in-depth medical tests on him.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:33.600
A few days after he was first brought in to
the research facility, a team of scientists

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.700
began to take various DNA samples.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.770
At first, the process went smoothly.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:42.620
They cut off a small piece of Cain’s hair,
swabbed his mouth for a saliva sample, and

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:45.510
scraped a few dead skin cells from the surface
of his arm.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:49.779
Then, with the man’s permission, they decided
to go a bit deeper and take some blood and

00:11:49.779 --> 00:11:51.370
tissue samples.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.730
This is where the trouble began.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.690
The researcher in charge of taking the blood
sample complained of a sudden sharp pain when

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:02.330
she pricked Cain’s arm with the needle,
occurring in the same part of her own arm.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.610
Nevertheless, she pushed through and took
a small vial of blood.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:10.310
However, when the blood was tested, it was
found to belong to a 40-year-old woman.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:14.380
Somehow, instead of drawing blood from the
test subject, the needle had filled the vial

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.610
with the researcher’s own blood.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:21.290
The research team tried again, with a different
doctor administering the blood test, but the

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.279
same thing happened again.

00:12:23.279 --> 00:12:24.310
And again.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.339
And again.

00:12:25.339 --> 00:12:29.240
Each time, the person taking the blood sample
somehow extracted a small amount of their

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:30.240
own blood.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:34.360
When the team attempted to take a small tissue
sample from Cain, cutting off a tiny portion

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:37.280
of skin with a scalpel, the same thing happened.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:42.350
Cain’s skin was left completely unharmed,
and the tissue sample wound up belonging to

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:44.720
the doctor who took it in the first place.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:48.600
Eventually, after a lot of trial and failure,
the head researcher declared that there would

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.820
be no more medical tests performed on SCP-073.

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:56.040
“If we keep going at this rate, we’re
going to have to organize a blood drive.”

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.680
He quipped, when pressed on the matter by
higher-ups.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:03.100
Why nobody asked him to take his own blood
is, to this day, a mystery.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:07.290
Because the attempts to test Cain’s blood
and other organic tissue had proven fruitless,

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:11.000
the research team turned their attention to
the more inorganic parts of his body.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:15.950
Namely, the portions of unidentified metal
located along his limbs, shoulder blades,

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:17.029
and spine.

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:20.680
After taking a closer look at the metal, one
research assistant suggested that it might

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:27.279
be beryllium bronze, a metal that has appeared
under a variety of other anomalous circumstances.

00:13:27.279 --> 00:13:32.731
SCP-073 confirmed that this metal originated
in the Middle East many many years ago, but

00:13:32.731 --> 00:13:37.480
was unable to provide an exact date, location,
or purpose of origin.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:42.589
Beryllium bronze has been identified as a
component in several SCPs so far, including

00:13:42.589 --> 00:13:50.180
SCP-1216, SCP-1427, SCP-2481, and SCP-2711.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:55.230
Further research into the unusual metal, and
its connection to many ancient civilizations,

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.240
is considered a top priority.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:02.330
Currently, Cain is kept at SCP Foundation
Site-17, where he is permitted to roam freely

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:06.860
as long as he does not leave the facility
or come into contact with any plant-based

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.150
SCPs, or plants of any kind.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:13.360
A new researcher that encountered Cain in
the Site asked him for his opinion on a bouquet

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:16.430
of flowers the researcher had purchased for
his wife.

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:20.341
Before Cain could protest, the researcher
had placed the bouquet in his hands, where

00:14:20.341 --> 00:14:24.540
it immediately disintegrated, much to the
distress of both men.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:29.250
Cain apologized profusely, and told the researcher
that he would offer to pay for a new bouquet,

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:31.890
but unfortunately, he did not have any money.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:36.100
A memo was sent out to all Site staff later
that day to remind them of Cain’s effect

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.839
on plant-based life forms.

00:14:37.839 --> 00:14:42.850
Due to the frequent staff turnover at SCP
Foundation sites, this reminder is issued

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:44.580
on a regular basis.

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:49.060
In addition to the reminder about plant life
exposure, Foundation staff are routinely reminded

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:55.160
that they must never use any violence against
SCP-073, under any circumstances.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:59.600
Great emphasis is placed on the fact that
this rule is for their own safety, not for

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:02.220
the safety of SCP-073.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:07.950
Though most of the staff know by now not to
deliberately harm SCP-073 in any way, accidents

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:12.210
still happen, and one careless moment could
result in unintentional self-injury.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:17.649
For example, one day Dr. Byer was having lunch
in the cafeteria, walking to his seat with

00:15:17.649 --> 00:15:22.450
his favorite dish: a steaming hot bowl of
tomato soup, with a grilled cheese sandwich

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:23.490
on the side.

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:27.490
He had specifically asked the kitchen staff
to make it as hot as possible, so that it

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:31.310
would still be warm when he had finished his
sandwich and several chapters of the book

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:33.120
he was reading on his break.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:38.660
As he passed SCP-073, who was enjoying a meal
of his own, Dr. Byer tripped and spilled his

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:41.869
scalding hot soup all over the man’s back.

00:15:41.869 --> 00:15:45.890
Before he could react, he fell to his knees
in pain as blisters and burns erupted across

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:47.260
his own back.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:51.370
Cain jumped up from the table with a surprised
yell, but his skin remained unblemished.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:55.560
Dr. Byer, on the other hand, had to spend
the rest of his lunch break in the medical

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.180
wing, and never got to finish that soup.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:02.399
Cain is permitted to interact with other SCPs,
as long as interaction between the two is

00:16:02.399 --> 00:16:06.079
not considered dangerous for one or more parties
involved.

00:16:06.079 --> 00:16:11.100
He has not expressed much interest in other
SCPs, with the exception of the few that are

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:13.910
also permitted to roam the facility as they
please.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:18.950
For example, he has engaged in some polite
small talk with SCP-507, and always gives

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:23.390
a friendly pat on the head to SCP-999 whenever
he bumps into it.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:31.050
There is one SCP, however, that Cain has specifically
requested he never be in a room with: SCP-076,

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.260
also known as Able.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:38.120
Though he has kept his personal knowledge
of SCP-076 to himself, Cain has admitted that

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:40.330
he knows everything about the man.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:44.160
He would not elaborate further, and simply
said that it would be better for everyone

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:46.160
involved if the two never met.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:50.720
No one knows for certain what would happen
if those two superhumans came face to face,

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:56.660
but, if someone as powerful as Cain is afraid
of the consequences, it certainly can’t

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.660
be good.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:05.150
Now go check out “SCP 073 &amp; 076 - Cain vs
Able” and “SCP-6008 - Noah's Ark” for

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.100
more epic anomalies!

